---
Implement dynamic range compressor effect.

Feed-forward compressor with sidechain detection.
Essential for tightening drum mixes and bus compression.

## Parameters
- threshold: Level where compression starts (-60 to 0 dB, default -20)
- ratio: Compression ratio (1:1 to 20:1, default 4:1)
- attack: Attack time (0.1-100 ms, default 10)
- release: Release time (10-1000 ms, default 100)
- makeup: Output gain (0-24 dB, default 0)
- wet: Wet/dry mix (0-1, default 1.0)

## Implementation
- RMS or peak envelope detection (configurable)
- Smooth gain computation with attack/release envelope
- Log-domain gain calculation
- Soft knee option (0-6 dB knee width)

## Acceptance Criteria
- [ ] EFFECT_COMPRESSOR added to effect type enum
- [ ] Reduces dynamic range above threshold
- [ ] Attack/release timing is accurate
- [ ] Makeup gain compensates for gain reduction
- [ ] Gain reduction amount available for metering

## Test Plan
- [ ] Loud signal compressed, quiet signal unaffected
- [ ] Fast attack catches transients
- [ ] Slow release creates pumping effect
- [ ] 1:1 ratio = no effect (passthrough)
